  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is Semantic HTML?</h2>
    <p><b>Semantic</b> means <b>meaningful</b>. Semantic HTML means using tags that <b>tell the meaning</b> of the content.</p>
    <p>In Lesson 8, we used <b>div</b> for everything. But div tells nothing. It just says "this is a box".</p>
    <p>Semantic tags tell the browser and Google - "This is a header", "This is navigation", "This is the main content", "This is the footer".</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> &lt;header&gt; = This is header | &lt;nav&gt; = This is menu | &lt;footer&gt; = This is footer. Google loves Semantic HTML, so it helps in SEO.</div>
    <h2>2. div vs Semantic - Easy Example</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- OLD WAY - With div (No Meaning) --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"header"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> My Website </span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"footer"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> © 2026 </span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- NEW WAY - Semantic (With Meaning) --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;header&gt;</span><span class="text"> My Website </span><span class="tag">&lt;/header&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;footer&gt;</span><span class="text"> © 2026 </span><span class="tag">&lt;/footer&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Both look the same.</b> But the second one is better for Google, for screen readers, and for other developers. Always use Semantic tags in real projects.</div>
    <h2>3. All Semantic Tags - Learn This Table</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Use For</th></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;header&gt;</td><td>Top Part</td><td>Logo, Title, Top Banner</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;nav&gt;</td><td>Navigation</td><td>Menu Links - Home, About, Contact</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;main&gt;</td><td>Main Content</td><td>Main content of the page - Only 1 per page</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;section&gt;</td><td>Section</td><td>One part - About Section, Services Section</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;article&gt;</td><td>Article</td><td>Blog post, News, Full story</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;aside&gt;</td><td>Side Content</td><td>Sidebar, Ads, Related Links</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;footer&gt;</td><td>Bottom Part</td><td>Copyright, Contact, Social Links</td></tr>
      <tr><td>&lt;figure&gt;</td><td>Figure</td><td>Image + Caption</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>4. Full Example - Complete Website Layout</h2>
    <p>This is how a professional website is made. Learn this structure:</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;header&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1&gt;</span><span class="text">My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;nav&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"#"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Home</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;a</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"#"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">About</span><span class="tag">&lt;/a&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/nav&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/header&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;main&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;section&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">About Me</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">I am learning HTML.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/section&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;article&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">My First Blog</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Today I learned Semantic HTML.</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/article&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;aside&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">Related Links</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/aside&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/main&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;footer&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="text">© 2026 My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/p&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/footer&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result">
      <b>Result - Website Layout:</b>
      <header class="demo-header"><b>My Website</b></header>
      <nav class="demo-nav">Home &nbsp; | &nbsp; About</nav>
      <main class="demo-main">
        <section class="demo-section"><b>About Me - section</b><br>I am learning HTML.</section>
        <section class="demo-section"><b>My First Blog - article</b><br>Today I learned Semantic HTML.</section>
        <div style="background:#fef3c7;padding:10px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0">Related Links - aside (sidebar)</div>
      </main>
      <div class="demo-footer">© 2026 My Website - footer</div>
    </div>
    <h2>5. section vs article - Confusing? Easy Trick</h2>
    <p><b>section</b> = A part of a page. Example: About Section, Services Section.<br><b>article</b> = A complete story that can stand alone. Example: One full blog post, one news story.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Trick:</b> If you can copy it and post it on another website and it still makes sense, it is an <b>article</b>. If it is just a part of the page, it is a <b>section</b>.</div>
    <h2>6. figure and figcaption - Image with Caption</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;figure&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;img</span> <span class="attr">src</span>=<span class="val">"my-photo.jpg"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;figcaption&gt;</span><span class="text">This is my photo</span><span class="tag">&lt;/figcaption&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/figure&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><figure style="margin:0;text-align:center;background:white;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#e2e8f0;padding:20px;border-radius:8px">🖼️ Image Here</div><figcaption style="margin-top:8px;color:#64748b">This is my photo</figcaption></figure></div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Create a page with:</p>
    <p>1. <b>header</b> with your name<br>2. <b>nav</b> with Home, About, Contact links<br>3. <b>main</b> with one <b>section</b> (About Me) + one <b>article</b> (My Blog)<br>4. <b>footer</b> with © 2026</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Semantic = Meaningful | header = Top | nav = Menu | main = Main Content (Only 1) | section = Part of page | article = Full blog / news | aside = Sidebar | footer = Bottom | figure + figcaption = Image + Caption | Semantic HTML = Better SEO + Better for Google</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson10">Lesson 10 - HTML Project 1</a> to build your first complete HTML project using everything you learned in Lesson 1 to 9.</p>
